 as you're going to get right now i don't  see any other way around that you know  and again yeah this is important stuff  yes there's so many guys in the nfl that  have you know a few hundred thousand  dollars uh associated with their  off-season workout program so uh they're  of course going to want to get that  money in the bank or at least make sure  that that's accounted for and i don't  know how that gets accomplished you know  it's going to be tough tough for new  players tough for the draft picks when  they come back into the league new  coaches right now with new organizations  certainly have an uphill climb to  indoctrinate their system within the  organization it's just not going to be  easy there's a lot of moving parts of  this football season it looks like  yeah and you know what you're going to  have and mike erfulo of nfl media had  the number last week 36 million roughly  speaking in workout bonuses that may or  may not be paid out and you know i hope  they find a way for the players to  qualify for that money or they take that  money and shift it into their salary or  they just do something to make the  players whole it's you know i don't  think the players should be the ones who  are victimized by the fact that they're  ready and able to show up and work out  but circumstances are preventing them  from doing it  can they you know the things i thought  of just brainstorming right like okay  just say i'm playing for the tampa bay  buccaneers you know can can the the can  the team  say something to the players as far as  like this mic like hey  quarterbacks  meet me at the practice field today  all right and you could still social  distance if there's only four or five  quarterbacks there can you put them  through the rigors of a workout and have  a strength coach stand 50 yards away and  bark out orders can you start doing  things like that mike would you be  frowned upon like say if they just  brought the db's in right and it was  just hey we got 12 dbs here here's the  strength coach he's going to stand on  the other field and you guys all spread  out 10 to 15 yards and we're gonna start  doing wind sprints is that a possibility  i mean i don't know am i crazy to think  that  well i i i don't think you're crazy to  think it the reality is in most states  where the nfl does business now we've  got stay-at-home orders so how do you  navigate that that's one of the issues  we're dealing with as it relates to the  draft trying to get i assume permission  from the various states where the nfl  does business to allow  up to 10 people to go to the facility  for the three days of the draft and  they're still  you know awkward optics with it too  because everybody else is staying home  right yes why why should the nfl get  special treatment when everybody else is  finding a way to deal with the  requirement to stay home now it's easy  for me to say because i do my job from  staying home anyway but i'm talking  about the millions out there who are  uh being truly hampered in their ability  to earn a living because they're  complying with the requirement to stay  home so that's one of the other twists  that i think needs to be considered if  the nfl wants to do something like that  you know we were ranting last week about  uh how the the pictures keep showing up  chris of guys who are finding a way to  work out and then they're draping their  arms around each other and taking a  photograph and how ridiculous that is  and how stupid that is and hopefully  hopefully guys find a way where they can  balance getting themselves in shape but  also complying with the requirements  that currently are applicable one last  quick point before we go how much do you  think this is going to hurt the new  coaches especially the first time  coaches there's only three of them kevin  stefanski joe judge and of course i knew  i'd forget the other one but oh matt  rule of the carolina panthers um how do  you think this is going to affect them  not having the ability to have an off  season program well we we've seen it's  doable right i mean we saw jim harbaugh  come in and be very successful his first  year with the san francisco 49ers i  think they went what 13 and three so it  can be done uh but  it's not gonna be easy and that was a  special circum set of circumstances that  jim harbaugh took over you know i look  at guys like joe judge and matt rule  uh where i go man first time head  coaches along with kevin stefanski and  there's a lot of team building that goes  has to go on there with those  organizations  i i think they're certainly way behind  more behind the eight ball than a guy  like mike mccarthy mike mccarthy ron  rivera been there done that but  especially mike mccarthy with the dallas  cowboys hey listen they got a lot of key  positions already in place for that  football team there's not a whole lot of  turnover with the dallas cowboys yeah  they need to do the new learn the new  offense and language and way of life and  all those things but nonetheless the  culture of players the the mainstay of  guys is still there and i would think  they would be a little less affected by  less than the  the panthers with bridgewater and  somebody or daniel jones in his second  year as a quarterback and a new coach  those are tougher obstacles to overcome  than dak prescott getting him in there  you already got ezekiel elliott amari  cooper and all these other proven  commodities  and the one advantage matt rule has  we've discussed this in the past with  this draft being watered down from the  standpoint yeah that's right you can  gather rule comes directly from the  world of college football and has  coached played against knows other guys  in the college coaching industry maybe  better than some nfl coaches at this  point and can tap into some of that  knowledge and that may give him a little  bit of an edge to balance out the  disadvantage of not having an offseason  program  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

